(188659, 10655, 3540, '<td valign="top">Critique Club by Inspzil<br/> <br/>Composition - I really like the colors of this image.  You took this pic at a great time.  The lighting is excellent really bringing out the colors.  The thing I notice most about this picture is the arch of the pier.  It could be used to frame the stuff behind it.  I think this would help in a couple of ways - First, it narrows the field of view which might bring a stronger focal point forward.  Secondly, I think switching it from portrait to landscape orientation will make it feel more natural.  I think there is too much unnecessary stuff in the frame.  I inspect these kind of bridge beams for a living.  I like to see them, but it isn''t necessary for this picture.<br/> <br/>Photography - Exposure is great.  The lighting had to be good there.  The colors are awesome.  The framing is the only thing that I would change about the whole picture. The rest of it is great.<br/> <br/>Processing - Nothing is standing out, so that''s good<br/> <br/>Overall - This is a pretty good picture with a lot of potential to be much better.  And I don''t think it would take too much.  Maybe even just a tighter crop and switching from portrait to landscape.  Hope this helps a little.  I enjoyed the shot. - Bob</td>', 'Critique Club by Inspzil Composition - I really like the colors of this image.  You took this pic at a great time.  The lighting is excellent really bringing out the colors.  The thing I notice most about this picture is the arch of the pier.  It could be used to frame the stuff behind it.  I think this would help in a couple of ways - First, it narrows the field of view which might bring a stronger focal point forward.  Secondly, I think switching it from portrait to landscape orientation will make it feel more natural.  I think there is too much unnecessary stuff in the frame.  I inspect these kind of bridge beams for a living.  I like to see them, but it isn''t necessary for this picture. Photography - Exposure is great.  The lighting had to be good there.  The colors are awesome.  The framing is the only thing that I would change about the whole picture. The rest of it is great. Processing - Nothing is standing out, so that''s good Overall - This is a pretty good picture with a lot of potential to be much better.  And I don''t think it would take too much.  Maybe even just a tighter crop and switching from portrait to landscape.  Hope this helps a little.  I enjoyed the shot. - Bob', '2003-01-13 09:15:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(188660, 10407, 5598, '<td valign="top">To all who commented, thank you!  However, those of you mentioning use of a 100.00 bill have never been hooked on drugs and never been close to it.  If a "user" has 100.00, it''s spent on drugs.  A more likely method would be a straw, smoked from a piece of aluminum foil or just tooted right off your hand with your nose.  An FYI, Clapton would have smoked it.  :)</td>', 'To all who commented, thank you!  However, those of you mentioning use of a 100.00 bill have never been hooked on drugs and never been close to it.  If a "user" has 100.00, it''s spent on drugs.  A more likely method would be a straw, smoked from a piece of aluminum foil or just tooted right off your hand with your nose.  An FYI, Clapton would have smoked it.  :)', '2003-01-13 09:17:04.000000', NULL, 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(188663, 10472, 2178, '<td valign="top">Great shot Mike, I saw the pic over at the DA site and loved it.</td>', 'Great shot Mike, I saw the pic over at the DA site and loved it.', '2003-01-13 09:24:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(188667, 10464, 4648, '<td valign="top">I thank each and everyone of you for your comments on my first submission.  This was taken in the back of the sanctuary of my church.  I was not happy with the background and made it B&amp;W to try to take your eyes off the background.  As for cutting off part of the arm of the cross, it is not.  It is right at the very tip of it.  I made it dark and softer with less contrast to set the mood of reaching to the cross in dark times. I really appreciate your time to comment and try to help me.</td>', 'I thank each and everyone of you for your comments on my first submission.  This was taken in the back of the sanctuary of my church.  I was not happy with the background and made it B&W to try to take your eyes off the background.  As for cutting off part of the arm of the cross, it is not.  It is right at the very tip of it.  I made it dark and softer with less contrast to set the mood of reaching to the cross in dark times. I really appreciate your time to comment and try to help me.', '2003-01-13 09:36:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(188729, 10653, 3889, '<td valign="top">Gracious --<br/> <br/>What a great idea.  This very well deserves a high ranking on the challenge.<br/> <br/>Big question -- Is that a multi-colored slinky that you used?<br/> <br/>Color is absolutely great.  The only thing that I would disagree on is the backlighting.  I''m not sure on the reddish cast.<br/> <br/>This is one picture that didn''t need to follow the rule of thirds!<br/> <br/>I could gush, and go on and on about what this picture has.  I love it so much, I am making it one of my favorites.<br/> <br/>Congrats on your placing in this week''s challenge.  It was so well deserved.<br/> <br/>-- shohn / DPC-CC</td>', 'Gracious -- What a great idea.  This very well deserves a high ranking on the challenge. Big question -- Is that a multi-colored slinky that you used? Color is absolutely great.  The only thing that I would disagree on is the backlighting.  I''m not sure on the reddish cast. This is one picture that didn''t need to follow the rule of thirds! I could gush, and go on and on about what this picture has.  I love it so much, I am making it one of my favorites. Congrats on your placing in this week''s challenge.  It was so well deserved. -- shohn / DPC-CC', '2003-01-13 10:34:16.000000', NULL, 0),
